.Dd August 30, 2026
.Dt AUTHORITYCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm authorityctl
.Nd capability-native control for the system authority
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the capability-native control tool for the system authority \(em the PID 1
spine
.Pq Xr authorityd 8 as Xr init 8 .
It is the parallel of
.Xr servicectl 8
for
.Xr serviced 8 :
it resolves the ADMIN-gated
.Dq Li system.lifecycle
capability over the ambient discovery plane a login session inherits, presents a
lifecycle request, and
.Xr serviced 8
relays it to the spine, which applies the transition.
.Pp
.Nm
sits
.Em beside
the traditional
.Xr reboot 8 ,
.Xr halt 8 ,
and
.Xr shutdown 8 ,
which keep their stock behaviour of signalling
.Xr init 8 .
Use
.Nm
for a capability-native shutdown, or from automation that already holds the
capability plane.
.Pp
The
.Ar command
is one of:
.Bl -tag -width "powercycle" -compact -offset indent
.It Cm reboot
Reboot the system.
.It Cm halt
Halt the system.
.It Cm poweroff
Halt and power off.
.It Cm powercycle
Power off, then power on.
.It Cm single
Bring the system to single-user.
.It Cm reroot
Re-root and restart
.Xr init 8 .
.It Cm rescan
Rescan
.Xr ttys 5 .
.It Cm catatonia
Quiesce for a fast, non-clean teardown.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A non-zero status is returned if the authority rejects the request (for example,
the caller does not hold the administrative right) or the capability plane is
unreachable.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr servicectl 8 ,
.Xr shutdown 8 ,
.Xr authorityd 8 ,
.Xr serviced 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
